course: dictionary
lesson: 11022
title: Waver: changing your mind
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: When someone wavers, they cannot decide, or they keep changing their mind. «The Rat sees how much the Mole wants it, and wavers.» The Rat has not decided yet, so he goes back and forth between yes and no.
explain: Read the clues around the word. «The Rat saw what was passing in his mind, and wavered.» The words «what was passing in his mind» tell you the Rat is thinking hard about two options. So waver must mean to be unsure. Try it: «The Rat was unsure, and was unsure» makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Waver has other meanings too. A flame can waver when a draught blows on it, and a voice can waver when someone is nervous. In each case, the clue tells you the thing is moving or shaking unsteadily, not thinking.
fact: Waver means to be unsure and keep changing your mind.
fact: «Wavered» is the past tense, and «wavering» is the -ing form.
fact: Waver can also mean to become weaker or less steady, as in «his courage wavered».
fact: A candle flame that wavers moves unsteadily, for example in a draught.
fact: «Unwavering» means steady and never changing, as in «unwavering loyalty».
exercise: «The Rat sees how much the Mole wants it, and wavers.» What does wavers mean here? | Falls fast asleep | Runs away quickly | *Is unsure and has not decided | Shouts very loudly
exercise: «The candle flame wavered in the draught.» What does wavered mean? | Stood perfectly still | Burned out for ever at once | Turned bright blue | *Moved unsteadily
exercise: What does «unwavering» loyalty mean? | *Loyalty that is steady and never changes | Loyalty that is shown loudly | Loyalty that is lost very quickly | Loyalty that only lasts a day
test: The hero's courage wavers when the dragon roars. What does wavers mean? | Goes to sleep | Grows much stronger | Makes a loud noise | *Becomes weaker or less steady
test: Her voice wavered as she read her name aloud. What does wavered mean here? | Rang out loud and clear | *Shook, showing she was nervous | Laughed at the joke | Sang a happy tune
exam: Toad's good promises always waver when he sees a motor car. What does waver mean here? | Toad writes his promises down | *Toad's promises become weak and he gives them up | Toad's promises get louder | Toad keeps every promise he makes
